ofing and siding products built-up roofing, modified roofing, EPDM roofing, PVC roofing, low-slope metal roofing TPO roofing, and commercial accessories; commercial waterproofing, concrete restoration and parking, public works, DOT and industrial, fire protection, wall systems, and safety and tools, as well as glass, glazing, and fenestration. In addition, it offers building materials; exterior and interior materials; and tools and equipment. The company provides its products under Atlas, Carlisle, CertainTeed, Elevate, Exterior Portfolio, GAF, IKO, James Hardie, LP SmartSide, Owens Corning, Royal, Tamko, TRI-BUILT, and Velux brands. It serves professional contractors, home builders, building owners, lumberyards, and retailers. The company was formerly known as SilverSun Technologies, Inc. and changed its name to QXO, Inc. in June 2024. QXO, Inc. is headquartered in Greenwich, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Bradley S. Jacobs | CEO & Chairman | Age 68 | Compensation: $750,000 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $878K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 59%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $24K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $19K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["QXO, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $13.1B market cap on $6.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +447% over the past three years and +74% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -2% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 40%.","The business throws off $183M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -1.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 47% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.46658377344516005},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 70/100): roic below cost of capital; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Peer Discount Creates Compelling Opportunity at QXO (QXO)","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/peer-discount-creates-compelling-opportunity-164546949.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794588346.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.863,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"QXO Inc. Reports 1.04 Billion Shares Outstanding in Q3 2026 SEC Filing","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/qxo-inc-reports-104-billion-shares-outstanding-in-q3-2026-sec-filing","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575370.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.735,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"QXO Reports Third Quarter 2026 Results","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/qxo-reports-third-quarter-2026-211500401.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794518100.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"QXO Appoints Dev Ahuja as CFO and Promotes Ihsan Essaid to Vice Chairman","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/qxo-appoints-dev-ahuja-as-cfo-and-promotes-ihsan-essaid-to-vice-chairman","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794482834.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.34,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"QXO Appoints Dev Ahuja as Chief Financial Officer and Promotes Ihsan Essaid to Vice Chairman","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/qxo-appoints-dev-ahuja-chief-110000103.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794481200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentimen